  {
    "id": "55",
    "bengali_name": "নন্দকিশোর চক্রবর্তী (রায়চৌধুরী)",
    "english_name": "Nanda Kishor Chakraborty (RoyChowdhury)",
    "dob": "",
    "doe": "",
    "photo": "",
    "details": "Nanda Kishor RoyChowdhury, the son of Harish Chandra RoyChowdhury tied a Shalagrama stone around his neck to escape the oppression of the Nawab, and fleeing at night along with a few caste members, came to the village of Mallikpur under Falta post of 24 Paraganas district and changed his surname, adopting the title of Chakraborty and settled there. One of his caste members also went and settled in the village of Mala. There are no descendants of his line remaining. Where the other caste members have settled, that is not known.",
    "father": "56",
    "mother": ""
  },
  {
    "id": "56",
    "bengali_name": "হরিশচন্দ্র রায়চৌধুরী",
    "english_name": "Harish Chandra RoyChowdhury",
    "dob": "",
    "doe": "",
    "photo": "",
    "details": "Lived at Geetgna (গীতগাঁ) under Burdwan district and belonged to the Ghritakaushik clan (গোত্র), a Baidik Brahmin by tradition. He had a son named Nanda Kishor RoyChowdhury, who later adopted the surname Chakraborty, marking the beginning of a new branch in the lineage.",
